---
/**
 * /policies/privacy — Privacy policy.
 * Static (prerendered). Written from what the code actually does (2026-11-12):
 * - Stripe Checkout collects name, email, phone, shipping address, payment (card never reaches us)
 * - stripe-webhook.ts sends name, email, phone, address to Printify (address_to)
 * - email.ts sends order-confirmation + shipped emails via SMTP2GO (name, email, order details, ship-to)
 * - cart = browser localStorage only; no analytics/ad cookies in our code; fonts self-hosted
 * - product images load from Printify's image servers; Cloudflare observability logs on
 * If any of that changes (analytics, newsletter, new processor), update this page + `updated`.
 */
import PolicyLayout from '../../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy"
  updated="November 12, 2026"
  description="PawnDepot privacy policy: what we collect, why, who we share it with, and your choices."
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    We collect only what we need to get your order to you. We don't sell your information, and we
    don't use ad trackers.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    When you check out, our payment processor Stripe collects your name, email, phone number,
    shipping address and payment details. We never see or store your full card number.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    To make, ship and support your order, and to email you about it: an order confirmation when
    you check out and tracking when it ships. We don't send marketing emails.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Stripe</strong> processes your payment (see <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Stripe's privacy policy</a>).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Printify and their print partners and shipping carriers</strong> receive your name,
      email, phone and shipping address to make and deliver your order.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>SMTP2GO</strong> sends our order and shipping emails, so it receives your name, email
      address and order details.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts our site and keeps short-term technical logs (like IP
      address and pages requested) for security and troubleshooting.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't sell or rent your personal information.</p>

  <h2>Cookies and your cart</h2>
  <p>
    Our site doesn't use advertising or analytics cookies. Your cart is saved in your own browser on
    your device, and you can clear it anytime. Stripe's checkout page may use its own cookies to
    process payments securely and prevent fraud.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep order records as long as needed for orders, support, and tax and accounting records.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:help@pawndepot.shop">help@pawndepot.shop</a> to ask what we have about you,
    or to correct or delete it. We may need to keep some records the law requires.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>PawnDepot isn't directed at children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their information.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we update this policy, we'll change the "Last updated" date above.</p>
</PolicyLayout>
